CORE
main.c
--unwind 3 --infer-rounds
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Infer rounds: violation found with 3 round
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^Infer rounds: violation found with [12] round
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The lost update of lazypo_lost_update_rounds_unsafe needs 3 rounds (it is
checked there with --rounds 3). --infer-rounds must find it at exactly 3:
fewer would mean the empty-round assumptions do not switch rounds off, and a
SUCCESSFUL would mean the completeness question stopped the search early --
which is what happened while the property was still asserted at the root of
the formula (symex_target_equationt::assertion_handles_only).
